body:
Looks like when using a small `texel_scale` the `atlas_size` ends up being smaller than `rendering/lightmapping/bake_performance/region_size` which is why it bakes successfully. 

I don't have any problem with reducing the default values for `rendering/lightmapping/bake_performance/region_size` and `rendering/lightmapping/bake_performance/max_rays_per_pass`

@Calinou Can you run some tests and get a feel for the bake time increase that results from decreasing `rendering/lightmapping/bake_performance/region_size` and `rendering/lightmapping/bake_performance/max_rays_per_pass`? IMO we should just reduce them to the lowest value we can without increasing the bake size significantly. Can you try to find out what those values would be?
